From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:45:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Count job 6017 as a mercenary

session_is_mercenary_or_homun_s_job took jobs 0x1782-0x17a4 (6018-6052).
The mercenary jobs are 6017-6046, MER_ARCHER01 (Mina) to MER_SWORDMAN10
(Wayne) in Hercules' mercenary_db.txt, and 6048-6052 are the
Homunculus S, so the first archer mercenary was left out. It now starts
at 0x1781.

What 6017 missed:

- game_actor_dir_of (position.c) shows a mercenary that stands, walks or
  is in action 0x10 in the 8-way direction rounded from its facing, as
  for players. Mina got the facing cut down instead, so for about half of
  all angles to the camera she showed the direction one below the one
  every other mercenary would show (40 degrees gave direction 0 instead
  of 1, and 340 degrees direction 7 instead of 0).
- skill_cast_target_look (skill_cast.c) and the merc AI GetV type 12 also
  ask the predicate, but neither changed for 6017: mercenaries arrive with
  object type 9, which the skill check accepts anyway, and GetV gives
  job % 0x1781 + 1, which is 1 for 6017, the value it gave her before.

Validation: the new test_mercenary_job runs the extracted predicate,
found by content because its name differs on purist, and
game_actor_dir_of: jobs 5990-6070 must be mercenaries exactly for
6017-6046 (and on main also 6047-6052), and every mercenary standing at
seven angles must show the same direction as job 6018, with 40 degrees
direction 1 and 340 degrees direction 0. 291 checks; the test fails on
the previous code. Release build without warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
